From b00815c0844bbbb95a65064941de10c0e041878c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:54:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(models): preserve invisible geometry and native defaults

Bedrock geometry can contain cubes with an empty UV face map. Omit these
cubes from Java model elements instead of inventing an unresolved texture
face or exporting an invalid element with no faces. Java 26.3 requires at
least one face per element; a wholly invisible model can have no elements.

Keep source bones and cubes available to the native renderer. Reindex
exported group children after filtering, and normalize copied UV arrays so
repeated export does not mutate cached model geometry.

Recorded CubeCraft turret, watermelon and gravestone models contain these
cubes. Synthetic tests cover mixed and wholly invisible geometry, valid
visible texture references, preserved source cubes and repeatable export.

An official Bedrock 1.26.51.1 capture of The Hive (protocol 2193) also
contains locator-only geometry with no cubes. Such a model accumulates no
bounds: fitting the initial extrema produces zero, and the reciprocal
becomes Infinity in conversion metadata. Use unit scale when no cube
contributes bounds while retaining cloned bones and source locator JSON.

Synthetic tests cover finite metadata serialization for empty geometry,
locator-only bone hierarchy and source preservation, every rotation mode,
and unchanged fitting for populated oversized geometry. All six focused
CubeConverter tests pass on Java 17.

The licensed Bedrock 1.26.51.1 models for leash knots, experience orbs,
fishing hooks, arrows, fireworks, tripods and fireballs omit cube UV data.
Treat an absent face map as empty instead of rejecting the whole model.
Keep cube bounds and valid neighboring cubes without inventing texture
faces. The mixed-cube parser and export regression covers this case.

Native 1.26.51.1 projectile planes also omit uv_size. Default its extent
to the declared cube face dimensions, preserving explicit signed sizes.
The versioned package supplies the cases; the official geometry schema
documents this optional default:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/minecraft/creator/reference/content/schemasreference/schemas/minecraftschema_geometry_1.21.0?view=minecraft-bedrock-experimental
Numeric tests cover all six asymmetric faces and an explicit negative size.

Retain geometry declarations that omit texture dimensions or the bones
array. The native geometry compiler supplies 64x64 defaults, and missing
bones describe an empty model. Dropping those declarations made invisible
Galaxite markers appear as unresolved geometry in the downstream resolver.
Legacy geometry keys also need those defaults; identify them by geometry.
prefix rather than requiring a texturewidth field.

Target Bedrock 1.26.51.1/protocol 2193 caller 141c11ba0 supplies width and
height 64 to compiler 141c13a30. A native instruction probe of its field
reader 141c13bfd..141c13c6b preserves caller defaults for absent/null fields
and overrides each dimension independently. The probe uses original JSON
lookup/integer helpers with exact host CRT and allocation boundaries; it
does not establish full model cache, schema dispatch or rendering parity.
Mojang's geometry 1.8.0 and 1.12.0 schemas mark dimensions and bones optional.

Preserve explicit dimensions and source JSON. Tests export modern and
legacy empty models through all Java rotation modes with finite unit scale,
including independent dimension overrides and a null dimension default.
